msgid "Fixed"
msgstr "修复"

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:24
msgid "Send each known Claude generation the thinking configuration it accepts. Extended thinking (`thinking.type = \"enabled\"` with `budget_tokens`) is rejected with a 400 from Claude 4.7 onward, so those models and the 4.6 generation now use adaptive thinking with `output_config.effort`, while Claude 4.5 and earlier keep their token budget; Opus 4.5 also receives its documented effort field. Unversioned gateway aliases remain unconfigured rather than being guessed as current-generation models. `/reason off` disables thinking where that is allowed and is omitted on the always-thinking families, which reject it."
msgstr "为每个已知 Claude generation 发送其接受的 thinking 配置。Claude 4.7 起会以 400 拒绝带 `budget_tokens` 的 extended thinking（`thinking.type = \"enabled\"`），因此这些模型和 4.6 generation 现在使用带 `output_config.effort` 的 adaptive thinking；Claude 4.5 及更早版本保留 token budget，Opus 4.5 还会收到其有文档支持的 effort 字段。无版本 gateway alias 保持不配置，不再猜测为当前 generation。`/reason off` 会在允许时关闭 thinking；对于会拒绝该设置的 always-thinking family 则省略。"

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:25
msgid "Echo Anthropic assistant turns back verbatim, thinking blocks and signatures included, as the Messages API requires for multi-turn and tool-use conversations; they were previously rebuilt from text and tool calls."
msgstr "按照 Messages API 对多轮和工具调用对话的要求，逐字回放 Anthropic assistant turn，包括 thinking block 和 signature；此前这些内容由 text 和 tool call 重建。"

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:26
msgid "Route OpenCode's GPT models to their documented Responses endpoint, alongside the existing Claude and Qwen routing to Messages."
msgstr "将 OpenCode 的 GPT 模型路由到有文档依据的 Responses endpoint，同时保留 Claude 和 Qwen 到 Messages 的现有路由。"

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:27
msgid "Apply the resolved provider policy to Responses requests too: reasoning effort uses the active protocol's documented mapping, GPT-5.1+ Responses models receive `none` for `/reason off`, unsupported off settings report an error instead of silently using the model default, and `temperature` is omitted for OpenAI reasoning models that reject it. Sibling chat models such as `gpt-4o` keep their sampling control."
msgstr "Responses 请求也使用解析后的 provider policy：reasoning effort 采用当前协议有文档依据的映射；GPT-5.1+ Responses 模型的 `/reason off` 收到 `none`；不支持的 off 设置会报错，不再静默使用模型默认值；对于会拒绝 `temperature` 的 OpenAI reasoning 模型则省略该字段。`gpt-4o` 等同级 chat 模型仍保留 sampling control。"

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:28
msgid "Accept every reasoning wire format `auto` can select as an explicit `chat_reasoning` value, so gateways and unrecognized model names keep a manual override; `thinking_toggle`, `thinking_effort`, and `mandatory_thinking` were previously resolvable but rejected by config validation."
msgstr "允许将 `auto` 能选择的每种 reasoning wire format 显式设为 `chat_reasoning`，使 gateway 和未识别的 model name 保留手动覆盖能力；此前 `thinking_toggle`、`thinking_effort` 和 `mandatory_thinking` 虽可被解析，却会被配置校验拒绝。"

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:29
msgid "Avoid double-counting visible assistant text and raw ciphertext/signature bytes in replayed provider items, while retaining readable Responses summaries and Anthropic thinking in the context estimate."
msgstr "避免在回放的 provider item 中重复计算可见 assistant text 和原始 ciphertext/signature byte，同时在 context 估算中保留可读的 Responses summary 和 Anthropic thinking。"

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:30
msgid "Drop saved reasoning items that carry no encrypted payload or readable summary instead of replaying an empty shell that a stateless request cannot resolve."
msgstr "丢弃既无 encrypted payload、也无可读 summary 的已保存 reasoning item，不再回放无状态请求无法解析的空壳。"

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:31
msgid "Omit `temperature` from Anthropic requests while thinking is enabled, which the Messages API rejects."
msgstr "Anthropic 请求启用 thinking 时省略 Messages API 会拒绝的 `temperature`。"

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:32
msgid "Preserve the CLI transcript after closing `/diff` by using the terminal's alternate screen; when tmux has alternate-screen support disabled, render the diff inline instead. The probe now reads the resolved window option, so the usual global `set -wg alternate-screen off` is detected and not just a per-window override."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:33
msgid "Restore both cache scopes in `/status`: the visual bar is now explicitly labeled `last`, while `last` and `session` each show cached tokens, prompt tokens, and hit rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:35
msgid "0.12.0 - 2026-07-21"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:38
msgid "Ctrl-C while the agent runs now distinguishes a *retract* from an *interrupt*. If the agent has not produced any output yet, the turn is retracted — the message is discarded and leaves no trace in the model context or the persisted session (the input history still recalls it via Ctrl-P), as if it was never sent. Once the agent has spoken or called a tool, the partial turn stands and an interrupt marker is appended (with a cancelled result for any tool call the interrupt left unanswered), so the context stays valid and the model knows the turn ended early."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:39
msgid "Fold completed Bash output into a quiet gray row instead of leaving its live preview in scrollback. `Ctrl-O` opens a newest-first browser for the ten most recent Bash previews, including persisted history after resume; select with `j`/`k` or arrows, open with `Enter`, return with `Esc`, and close with `Ctrl-O` or `q`. Blank rows separate live output from the working divider and each viewer's subdued labeled rule from scrollback. Full results remain stored under their `tr.N` keys."
msgstr "完成的 Bash 输出会折叠为安静的灰色行，不再将实时预览留在终端回滚缓冲区中。`Ctrl-O` 会打开按从新到旧排列的最近十次 Bash 预览浏览器，其中也包含 resume 后恢复的历史记录；使用 `j`/`k` 或方向键选择，按 `Enter` 打开，按 `Esc` 返回，按 `Ctrl-O` 或 `q` 关闭。空行会将实时输出与 working 分隔线隔开，也会将每个 viewer 的低调带标签分隔线与终端回滚内容隔开。完整结果仍保存在对应的 `tr.N` key 下。"

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:42
msgid "Background jobs (`Job(start)`) now capture every stage of a compound command such as `configure && make && pytest`; previously only the final stage was logged and earlier output leaked to the terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:43
msgid "Opening the external editor no longer truncates a draft at a git-style scissors line you typed yourself — only the reference context minacode appends below its own marker is stripped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:46
msgid "0.11.0 - 2026-07-20"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:49
msgid "Ctrl-X Ctrl-E (and Ctrl-G) now opens the external editor with the agent's most recent reply appended below a git-style scissors line, so you can read what you are answering while you compose; everything from the scissors line down is stripped before the message is sent. Long replies are capped to their most recent lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:50
msgid "Show a placeholder tip in the idle input while it is empty, picked at random for the session from a few shortcuts (`Ctrl-X Ctrl-E opens $EDITOR`, `Type / for commands`, `Ctrl-U clears the line`) so they stay discoverable without cluttering the prompt; it disappears as soon as you start typing and gives way to the queue hints while the agent runs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:53
msgid "Renamed the project from `nanocode` to `minacode`: the package and import (`import minacode`), the `minacode` console script and `python -m minacode`, and the PyPI distribution (`minacode`, formerly `nanocode-cli`). The data dir moved from `~/.nanocode` to `~/.minacode`; when the new directory is absent the old one is still read, so existing sessions, skills, and config keep working without a migration step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:54
msgid "Split the single `nanocode.py` module into a `minacode` package of focused submodules — `base`, `session`, `skill`, `mcp`, `tools`, `engine`, `tui` — plus a `__main__` entry module (so `python -m minacode` now works alongside the `minacode` console script), all re-exported through `minacode/__init__.py` so `import minacode` keeps exposing the same namespace as before. Module-internal helpers (`_read_and_release`, `_validate_edit_target`, `_resolved_tool_schemas`) are underscore-prefixed and gathered at the bottom of `tools.py`. Behavior, the CLI entry point, and the public API are otherwise unchanged; this reorganizes the source so it is easier to navigate and to trim optional features later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:55
msgid "Ask previews now ask for concrete graphic content (snippets, directory trees, file shapes) instead of restating the choice label, with the built-in example updated to match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:58
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Run background job commands directly under `bash -lc` instead of `exec {command}`. The `exec` prefix failed for shell builtins and compound commands (`cd dir && cmd`) with `exec: cd: not found`; `start_new_session` already makes the shell the process-group leader, so `killpg` still reaches the command and its children."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:61
msgid "0.10.0 - 2026-07-19"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:64
msgid "Clear the whole input line with `Ctrl-U`, in the idle prompt, the follow-up editor, and approval prompts alike. `Ctrl-C` keeps its existing meanings, including interrupting a running turn, so clearing a draft never competes with stopping the agent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:65
msgid "Replay the diff each `Edit` made when a session is resumed, instead of only the call line. Long diffs are trimmed to a readable window with a pointer to `/diff`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:66
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Add a `provider.extra_body` option (a JSON object, default empty) merged verbatim into the outgoing chat request's `extra_body`, so provider-specific extensions reach the wire without nanocode knowing about them. This is how a server-side built-in capability such as Qianwen/DashScope web search is enabled (`{\"enable_search\": true, \"search_options\": {...}}` against `https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1`). nanocode's own reasoning fields are layered on top, so they stay authoritative on key conflicts, and the configured value is surfaced in `/config`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:69
msgid "Let `Ctrl-C` discard a draft in the follow-up editor. It previously interrupted the turn and left the draft in place, so there was no way to clear a half-typed follow-up while the agent worked. With the editor empty it still interrupts, which is exactly when the `Ctrl-C interrupts` hint is shown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:70
msgid "Apply the `/diff` snapshot size limit to each file snapshot rather than to the before-and-after pair. Snapshots are stored once per unique content, so the pair no longer costs twice a file's size, and the old test held the ceiling at half the file size it could afford — files up to roughly 1 MB are now tracked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:71
msgid "Store sessions per project under `<data_dir>/projects/<project>/`, each with its own `latest` pointer, instead of a single flat `<data_dir>/sessions/` directory shared by every project. Resolving this project's latest session is now a pointer read rather than a scan that opens every stored session, and a project directory is pruned once its last session expires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:72
msgid "Scope `--resume latest` and `--resume last` to the current project. They previously resolved a single global pointer and could resume a session belonging to a different directory; they now behave like `-c`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:73
msgid "Begin each session log with a header line recording the format version, UID, working directory, and creation time. The version gate turns an unreadable log into a clear error instead of a misparse, and the log describes itself when read by hand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:74
msgid "Store the file snapshots behind `/diff` by content hash instead of inline in every edit record. Editing one file repeatedly stored each version twice, once as an edit's `after` and again as the next edit's `before`; each version is now written to the log once. Past 100 edits, where every save rewrites the whole retained window, a save rewrote every snapshot again — it now rewrites only the references."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:77
msgid "Persist the session immediately after `/compact`. The compacted history lived only in memory until the next turn, so leaving the session right after compacting resumed from the pre-compaction log."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:78
#, python-format
msgid "Recompute the context percentage when a session is resumed. The value is derived rather than persisted, so the status bar read `ctx 0%` on a restored session until its first turn — a session actually sitting at 100% looked empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:79
msgid "Summarize the work that followed the current request during `/compact`, not just the conversation before it. One request can drive dozens of tool calls, and keeping that tail whole left the context nearly as large as it started — compacting a 93-message session summarized 47 messages holding 101k characters while keeping 46 messages holding 209k, so the context stayed at 43%."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:80
msgid "Show one diff per file in `/diff` when a file's edits are only partly covered by stored snapshots, which happens once a file grows past the snapshot size limit mid-session. The snapshot-derived diff and the reconstructed one were both emitted, repeating the file's changes under two headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:81
msgid "Isolate `HOME` in the test suite. Tests that built a config without an explicit `paths.data_dir` and then saved a session wrote into the developer's real `~/.nanocode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:82
msgid "Describe `Ctrl-C` in the running follow-up hint as interrupting the turn rather than \"sending immediately\". `Ctrl-C` interrupts the current task and keeps any draft in the editor; it does not submit the draft, so the previous hint advertised an action that does not exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:84 ../../../CHANGELOG.md:93 ../../../CHANGELOG.md:115
msgid "Removed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:85
msgid "Drop reading of pre-existing session files. Sessions written by earlier versions are not migrated and are no longer loadable; `<data_dir>/sessions/` can be deleted. This also removes the recovery of edit diffs from legacy `Edit` tool records and the tolerance for retired cache-prefix state keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:88
msgid "0.9.11 - 2026-07-19"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:91
msgid "Discover `auto_connect` MCP servers in the background at startup, so an unreachable server no longer holds up the prompt for the discovery timeout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:94
msgid "Remove the undocumented `runtime.max_steps` configuration alias; set `runtime.max_agent_steps` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:97
msgid "0.9.10 - 2026-07-18"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:100
msgid "Add `g`/`G` jumps to the top/bottom in the `/diff` viewer and interactive selectors, matching the `less` pager convention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:101
msgid "Add an interactive `/mcp` connection manager and per-server `auto_connect` configuration for explicit startup connections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:104
msgid "Replace the in-flight model retry keybinding with `/resend` in the running follow-up input, and show a `/resend` hint during long requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CHANGELOG.md:105
